+# Agent Note: Market development homepage
+
+Status: implemented
+
+## Problem
+
+Market monitoring needs to occupy the dsh primary desktop window while retaining access to dsh conversations. A separate companion window does not satisfy that workflow.
+
+## Decision
+
+An unpackaged Desktop shell uses the explicitly configured Market Agent checkout for four allowlisted static assets. Its main window defaults to the market page. An isolated preload offers named API operations; main-process sender and frame checks guard a fixed loopback service with a token loaded outside the renderer. Application menu actions switch the same window between market and conversation pages. Packaged shells ignore the development override.
+
+## Alternatives considered
+
+**Separate Electron companion:** rejected because monitoring must be the primary dsh page. **A general renderer HTTP proxy:** rejected because the UI needs only five named operations and no token access.
+
+## Consequences
+
+The dsh agent and conversation implementation stays intact, while release packaging must explicitly include the market assets and backend. The patch is maintained against the pinned upstream revision. Focused tests reject unknown files, foreign webContents, child frames and invalid operation payloads; the Desktop TypeScript and shell build validate integration.
